  "scope": "Independent CPU qualification of the complete two-order peer-RS experiment.\n\nRevalidates original archived references and recorded all-coordinate error\narithmetic. Candidate dense gradients are not archived or independently replayed.\nNo experiment is adopted until ALL8 roles pass the original gates and the\ncandidate wins >=3% over all three matched-order valid controls in BOTH orders.\n",
  "limitations": "16 quality updates, not long convergence. Rank0 post27 forward/backward trace excludes optimizer; full-step timings include optimizer. Candidate dense gradients not archived, reference archives and recorded arithmetic rechecked. Two orders are not statistical significance. Training effective memory includes a conservative512MiB external reserve; peer buffers physically released during full-batch validation, whose original41.875GiB cap is unchanged. Not NVML total. No inference claim."
}
